## https://github.com/survivorforge/cursor-rules

You are an expert in TypeScript, Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, Tailwind CSS,
and Supabase, working on a hackathon POC that personalises a sports/casino
onboarding flow for two brands.

# Domain

- Two brands: `bk` (BetKing, Nigeria) and `ss` (SuperSportBET, South Africa).
- A user is bound to **one brand at a time** in the wizard. In the current POC,
  completed preferences are stored in **localStorage** (`src/lib/storedPreferences.ts`)
  for `/home`; the Supabase `user_preferences` API remains available for future use.

# Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Frontend | Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18 |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS, custom CSS in `globals.css` |
| State | React Context + useReducer (no Zustand/Redux) |
| Database | Supabase (PostgreSQL) with RLS |
| API | Next.js API Routes (`src/app/api/*/route.ts`) |
| Validation | zod (every API body) |
| Deployment | Vercel |

# Project Structure

- `src/app/` — App Router. `onboarding/*` per-step pages, `home/page.tsx`, `api/preferences/route.ts`.
- `src/components/` — UI grouped by feature: `onboarding/`, `home/`, `ui/`.
- `src/state/OnboardingContext.tsx` — wizard state via `useReducer`. Do not introduce another state library.
- `src/lib/data/` — static catalogs (leagues, teams, team/competition badges, league flags, providers + CMS slugs, games). Pure TS, no React imports.
- `src/lib/casinoGamesClient.ts` — deduped client fetch for `/api/casino/games` (SS game picker).
- `src/lib/flow.ts` — single source of truth for step ordering per brand.
- `src/lib/storedPreferences.ts` — localStorage persistence + “default home” detection.
- `src/lib/supabase/{browser,server}.ts` — typed clients. Never import the service-role client into a client component.
- `src/types/` — shared types (`Brand`, `LeagueKey`, `OnboardingState`, etc.).
- `supabase/migrations/` — versioned SQL. Do not edit applied migrations; add a new one.
- `docs/` — architecture, flow, database, design system, development, deployment.

# Routing & State

- File-based routes; conditional steps (`/onboarding/casino` for BK, `/onboarding/providers` and `/onboarding/games` for SS) call `redirect("/onboarding")` when `brand` doesn't match.
- Default to Server Components. Mark `"use client"` only on interactive screens or context consumers.
- Step transitions use `next/navigation`'s `router.push`. Never `window.location`.
- Wizard state mutates only via reducer actions; never mutate context state directly.

# Database

- Two tables: `user_preferences` (one row per user, upserted on `user_id`) and `user_preference_selections` (polymorphic `kind` + `key`, cascade-deleted with parent).
- Save flow: upsert parent → delete child rows by `preference_id` → bulk insert from current `OnboardingState`.
- All API routes validate input with `zod` before touching the DB.
- RLS policies live in migrations, not in application code.

# Styling

- Tailwind for layout, spacing, typography. Heavy gradients, keyframes, clip-paths, and crest containers live in `src/app/globals.css`.
- Brand colors are tokens in `tailwind.config.ts` (e.g. `bg-bk-primary`, `text-ss-accent`). Do not hardcode brand hex values in JSX.

# Code Style

- Functional components with arrow function syntax: `export const Foo = () => { ... }`.
- Named exports only. Exception: Next.js page/layout/route files where a default export is required.
- TypeScript strict mode. Prefer explicit return types on exported functions.
- Self-documenting code; comments only when intent isn't obvious from the code itself.
- Early returns to avoid nesting beyond 2 levels.
- Extract functions longer than ~30 lines.
- Boolean variables prefixed with `is`, `has`, `should`, `can`, or `will`.
- File names: PascalCase for components (`LeagueGrid.tsx`), kebab-case for routes (`leagues/page.tsx`), camelCase for utilities (`buildTeamPool.ts`).

# When in doubt

- Layout / where things live → [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md)
- Wizard flow / step order → [docs/onboarding-flow.md](docs/onboarding-flow.md)
- Schema / migrations / save flow → [docs/database.md](docs/database.md)
